    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95584" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σολοικ-ισμός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>incorrectness in the use of
				language, solecism</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>SE</u>
				173b17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σολοικισμοὶ καὶ βαρβαρισμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.159
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.731f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρβαρισμός</span>,
			incorrectness in the use of words, is distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σολ</span>., <i>incorrectness in the construction of
				sentences</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				198.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.159
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of incorrect reasoning,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ σολοικισμῶν</span>, title of
			work by Chrysippus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>; cf.foreg. <i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>awkwardness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.520b
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
